= Rumored Emergency Decree

It is rumored that by the end of last month, Chancellor von Goodryke secured DuFour's approval for two emergency decrees: one to dissolve the Assembly, and another—blatantly unconstitutional—to postpone elections beyond the 60-day limit mandated by the Unity Constitution. These decrees would allow Goodryke to govern unchallenged, free from the threat of parliamentary repeal or a vote of no confidence.

Goodryke has quickly become DuFour’s favorite, and the president—unwilling to part with him—has signed off on a decree that violates the constitution he swore to uphold. Former Chancellor Askew, upon learning of this, has threatened DuFour with impeachment should he proceed, persuading himself that he'd deterred Goodryke from presenting the decree in the next session.